<title>USA: Compaq's Microcom cuts modem prices.</title>
<headline>Compaq's Microcom cuts modem prices.</headline>
<dateline>NORWOOD, Mass. 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microcom Inc, a unit of Compaq Computer Corp, on Wednesday said it cut prices for its family of stand-alone modem products by an average of 40 percent in the U.S. and Canada.</p>
<p>The companies recent merger with Compaq gives Microcom volume cost reductions in manufacturing and increased channel distribution, Microcom said. Both of these factors allow Microcom to lower its price.</p>
<p>The company's new list prices for the Microcom stand-alone modems range from $99 to $370, but they estimated that prices at retail will range from $60 and $250.</p>
<p>For example, the DeskPorte S 33.6 modem, whose list prices fell to $99 from $276, is estimated to sell between $60 and $70, the company said.</p>
</text>
